5
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.130
returning for his second appearance on the show,

6
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.230
his first being almost exactly three years ago.

7
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.080
That was episode 351,

8
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.450
if you missed it on the first go around.

9
00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.930
Most of all of you are familiar at this point

10
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.630
with Alex's death and gravity-defying, ropeless ascent

11
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.800
of El Capitan on the big screen.

12
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.080
That was a feat that landed the film "Free Solo"

13
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.520
a documentary Oscar, of course,

14
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.390
and also cemented Alex in the history books

15
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.340
as truly one of the greatest athletes of all time.

16
00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:43.210
This conversation picks up where our last one left off

17
00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.490
to explore some of Alex's life experiences

18
00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:49.900
and interests post "Free Solo" as an adventurer,

19
00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.360
as the co-host

20
00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.240
of the recently released Climbing Gold podcast,

21
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.720
also as an environmentalist at the helm

22
00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.500
of the Honnold Foundation and many other topics.

23
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.780
It's such a good one,

24
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.630
definitely quite a bit different

25
00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.620
from other conversations with Alex

26
00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.910
that you might have enjoyed over the years.

27
00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:12.080
So without further ado, let's do the thing.

28
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.814
This is me and the great Alex Honnold.

29
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.140
Cool man. Are we good?
All good.

30
00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.894
Oh, we're rolling. Excellent, man.

31
00:01:25.894 --> 00:01:27.360
Oh, we're recording?

32
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.300
Yeah, we're already recording.

33
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.290
Good to see you.
Yeah, good to see you.

34
00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.940
Do I need to worry about where anything is or?

35
00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:32.773
I don't think so.

36
00:01:32.773 --> 00:01:34.330
Just worry about where the mic is,

37
00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:35.163
But you know that,

38
00:01:35.163 --> 00:01:36.550
because now you're a professional podcaster.

39
00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.796 line:15%
Well, I don't really do the technical side of it.

40
00:01:39.796 --> 00:01:40.993 line:15%
(Rich laughs)

41
00:01:40.993 --> 00:01:42.530 line:15%
You do have to talk into a mic though?

42
00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:44.340 line:15%
I bring nothing to the team

43
00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.720
except for the witty banter with the guests.

44
00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.260
Well, I listened to like the first little,

45
00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.110
like the little trailer thing and it's all,

46
00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.470
you do the little like, "Hey, is this thing on?"

47
00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.800
Or like, "Let's do take two" or whatever.

48
00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.730
I actually, I don't know if I've heard it yet.

49
00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:58.810
You haven't, oh, you haven't even listened

50
00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.773
to your own podcast yet?

51
00:02:00.773 --> 00:02:02.287
Well, I've been gone.

52
00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:04.650
But the idea, I mean, it's called Climbing Gold.

53
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.390
The idea, was the idea at the inception

54
00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.670
that it was gonna be more

55
00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:12.070
about the Olympics and then that had to pivot a little bit?

56
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:12.903
Yeah, exactly.

57
00:02:12.903 --> 00:02:16.100
The idea for the podcast was to focus on the road

58
00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.900
to the Olympics, sort of the buildup,

59
00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:20.330
because going into 2020,

60
00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:22.730
it felt like climbing was having a huge moment.

61
00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.230
It's funny, I'm on the board

62
00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.830
of a climbing gym organization as well,

63
00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.118
and it felt like it was this huge moment for climbing,

64
00:02:29.118 --> 00:02:30.080
'cause climbing is in the Olympics

65
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:30.913
for the first time.

66
00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:32.250
And it's like going off.

67
00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.920
Obviously COVID changed that quite a bit.

68
00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.890
And so when we started talking about doing a podcast,

69
00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:40.310
it made sense to explore sort of the history

70
00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:43.210
and the future of climbing during this moment.

71
00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:45.494
And then when the Olympics got pushed because of COVID,

72
00:02:45.494 --> 00:02:47.990
we sort of went forward with it anyway,

73
00:02:47.990 --> 00:02:49.110
mostly because we felt

74
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.420
like there were still interesting stories to tell.

75
00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.190
But so now we're still doing,

76
00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.320
I think we're doing 20 episodes,

77
00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.470
and the second 10 are focused more on the lead up

78
00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.499
to the Olympics, which we'll be doing this summer.

79
00:02:59.499 --> 00:03:01.220
So it's sort of like the history

80
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.450
and the untold stories and the kind of things that happen.

81
00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.560
Because so much of climbing occurs outside

82
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.820
of the spotlight of the media completely.

83
00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.020
Well, and so much of climbing history has occurred

84
00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:12.930
before there was media to some extent, you know,

85
00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:17.310
before things were easily recorded or digified and shared.

86
00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.150
And so there are just so many classic climbing stories

87
00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:22.260
that are sort of lost to history a little bit.

88
00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.410
So it's pretty fun to uncover some

89
00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.870
of those and share some.

90
00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.780
So did you have to be like a journalist

91
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.220
and go and find these people

92
00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.810
and talk to them and have them tell their stories?

93
00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.990
Like a very unprofessional journalist,

94
00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.913
like a very unskilled journalist.

95
00:03:36.913 --> 00:03:38.780
A podcaster.
Yeah, exactly, exactly.

96
00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.348
Yeah, quote podcaster.
Let's not confuse

97
00:03:40.348 --> 00:03:42.360
journalism with podcasting.
Yeah, exactly, exactly.

98
00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.540
No, it's not fair to say

99
00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.680
that we did any journalism,

100
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.830
but we did seek out interesting guests in different spaces.

101
00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.150
And I think the thing that we're trying to sort of add

102
00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.811
to the space of climbing podcasting as it were

103
00:03:54.811 --> 00:03:58.760
is a little bit more editing and a little bit more

104
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.180
of a thematic focus, like, you know, having multiple voices

105
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.040
from different people in the same episode

106
00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:05.560
talking about specific themes

107
00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.790
to sort of help educate about certain aspects of climbing

108
00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.073
and share a little bit about where climbing has come from.

109
00:04:12.073 --> 00:04:16.270
And your cohost has, he did another podcast, right?

110
00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.930
Dirtbag Diaries or something like that?

111
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.670
Yeah, my cohost is Fitz Cahall

112
00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.000
who's an actual professional podcaster.

113
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.060
He actually knows what he's doing.

114
00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.050
He's the one that sent me the microphone that I use

115
00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.750
and told me how to set it up and how to use everything.

116
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:30.472
Yeah, he's the one that really...

117
00:04:30.472 --> 00:04:33.720
And I mean, really the whole reason the podcast exists

118
00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.320
is because he approached me

119
00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.890
about working on a project together.

120
00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.250
And I was like, "Oh, he's the perfect person to work with,

121
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.320
"because he already knows how to do it."

122
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.540
Was there an original plan before the Olympics got pushed

123
00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:45.650
that you would go to Tokyo and be,

124
00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.680
make covering the climbing competition there

125
00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:50.720
part of the podcast?

126
00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.255
No, so fun story.

127
00:04:52.255 --> 00:04:53.870
I am actually supposed to be going

128
00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:56.480
to Tokyo to do commentary for the Olympic Channel.

129
00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.790
So technically I have a contract already

130
00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.940
with the actual Olympic Committee or whatever to go

131
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.370
do commentary for climbing.
To do that.

132
00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:04.940
And so part of doing the podcast was

133
00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:05.880
because I personally felt

134
00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.680
like it would be a great way to learn how to commentate.

135
00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.000
Because I don't know anything about sports commentation,

136
00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.600
but I figured I'd learn before the Olympics.

137
00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.850
And so the podcast seemed

138
00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:16.650
like a really great way to get to know some

139
00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.020
of the backstory, meet some of the competitors,

140
00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:21.190
learn about their process.

141
00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.930
And you know, so as it turns out,

142
00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.800
we haven't focused on that so far,

143
00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.540
because the Olympics got pushed.

144
00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:30.020
So we just decided to kind of wait and see on that side.

145
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:30.970
But it's almost better this way,

146
00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.010
because this way the episodes that we have recorded

147
00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.540
are like the deeper backstory

148
00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.150
and then it allows us to sort of set the stage

149
00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:39.090
so that when we get to the Olympic side of the podcast

150
00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.326
there's already a good context for it.

151
00:05:40.326 --> 00:05:41.160
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

152
00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:44.040
So somebody who doesn't know anything can listen to that,

153
00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.000
and then by the time the competition starts,

154
00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.500
they feel like they have a context-

155
00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:48.333
Exactly.

156
00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:49.166
For everything that's happening.

157
00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:50.850
That's exactly the hope is that someone

158
00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.400
who's interested in the outdoors

159
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.490
and has maybe climbed once or, you know,

160
00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:57.508
just sort of a general interest could listen to the podcast,

161
00:05:57.508 --> 00:05:59.810
understand and appreciate the stories

162
00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.890
and still feel like they learned something important

163
00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:03.547
about the sport.

164
00:06:03.547 --> 00:06:05.890
How do you feel in general

165
00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:08.530
about climbing being in the Olympics?

166
00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.460
I'm pretty into it.

167
00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.990
I mean, there are a lot of climbers,

168
00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.160
particularly older climbers

169
00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.220
that are sort of crusty about it

170
00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.840
that think that it's, you know, degrades the sport

171
00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:17.920
in some way or sort of,

172
00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.920
or really the fact that I'm calling climbing a sport.

173
00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.500
I think some climbers would take umbrage with that.

174
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.490
Because a lot of people consider climbing more

175
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.333
of a lifestyle or more of like an adventure.

176
00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.790
But you know, I come from a gym climbing background.

177
00:06:31.790 --> 00:06:32.950
I grew up going to a climbing gym.

178
00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.988
So I've always thought of climbing

179
00:06:34.988 --> 00:06:37.240
at least in some part as a sport.

180
00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.133
And so I'm excited about the Olympics.

181
00:06:39.133 --> 00:06:40.530
I mean, I'm psyched to go.

182
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.730
I'm psyched to see it.

183
00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.520
I saw a rendering of the venue.

184
00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.738
It looked incredible.
I haven't seen it yet.

185
00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:47.170
It's like this huge like amphitheater

186
00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.510
with the walls and like, you know, the seating.

187
00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:50.343
Cool.

188
00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.560
I don't know what it's gonna be like

189
00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:55.640
now that they're restricting kind of attendance, right?

190
00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.690
Like if you're a foreigner you can't go or-

191
00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:59.730
I think there'd be enough domestic attendance

192
00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:00.857
that it'll still be crazy.

193
00:07:00.857 --> 00:07:03.140
I mean, climbing in Japan is a big deal.

194
00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.760
Is it?
Yeah, it's really popular.

195
00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:07.040
And Japanese competitors have sort of dominated

196
00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.010
the World Cup scene for the last few years,

197
00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:10.610
which I think is maybe part of the reason

198
00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:14.320
that climbing is in the Olympics in Tokyo this year is

199
00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.290
because I think the host country has some influence on that.

200
00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:21.230
But yeah, Japanese competitors will likely do very well

201
00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.430
and will likely have enthusiastic support

202
00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.945
from the home crowd.

203
00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:30.340
Well, what's interesting about it now being a sport,

204
00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.303
where there's the controversy of it being a sport

205
00:07:32.303 --> 00:07:36.030
to begin with and then there's controversy around

206
00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.580
how they're constructing the competition, right?

207
00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:41.290
Like you have these three events essentially,

208
00:07:41.290 --> 00:07:43.840
like speed, boulder, lead,

209
00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.450
and it's kind of your cumulative score

210
00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:50.220
across those three disciplines that determines your ranking.

211
00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:51.347
Yeah, that's exactly it.

212
00:07:51.347 --> 00:07:55.890
And so it's a slightly confused system in some ways.

213
00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:56.930
I mean, I think it's fine.

214
00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.930
It skews towards doing it fast though, right,

215
00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.755
which is kind of a weird thing, isn't it?

216
00:08:00.755 --> 00:08:01.964
No, sort of.

217
00:08:01.964 --> 00:08:03.750
It's like, should we just dive into it?

218
00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:04.820
It's like slightly complicated.

219
00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:05.653
Yeah, yeah.

220
00:08:05.653 --> 00:08:06.770
Like, I mean, this is like inside baseball,

221
00:08:06.770 --> 00:08:07.700
but this is interesting,

222
00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.820
and especially since the Olympics are going to be happening

223
00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.120
and we're all gonna be watching this.

224
00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:12.670
And actually, so yeah, I'll dive into

225
00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:15.220
like the nitty gritty of climbing scoring.

226
00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.780
But I think what's interesting about it is

227
00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.610
that you can kind of apply this to all sports,

228
00:08:18.610 --> 00:08:21.258
because the decathlete or the biathlon or whatever,

229
00:08:21.258 --> 00:08:22.830
like to some extent any sport you see

230
00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:24.793
in the Olympics is being arbitrarily scored

231
00:08:24.793 --> 00:08:26.783
in a way that the competitors

232
00:08:26.783 --> 00:08:30.320
or at least the organizing committees have agreed upon.

233
00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.440
And so, you know,

234
00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.908
any sport that you're watching is slightly arbitrary.

235
00:08:33.908 --> 00:08:38.120
I mean, other than just the purely elemental swimming

236
00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.090
or running, like strictly for speed.

237
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:40.923
Other than that,

238
00:08:40.923 --> 00:08:42.610
you're always getting into formatting issues

239
00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:46.500
and it's just interesting.

240
00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:49.790
And so with climbing, like you said,

241
00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.290
it's the combination of the three disciplines.

242
00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.266
It's a combined format.

243
00:08:52.266 --> 00:08:56.450
But it's actually, you multiply the scores in them.

244
00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:00.560
And so it sort of disproportionately weights excellence

245
00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.363
in specific categories in a weird way.

246
00:09:02.363 --> 00:09:03.519
You know what I mean?

247
00:09:03.519 --> 00:09:05.620
In theory if someone's average,

248
00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.410
if someone's pretty good at all three disciplines,

249
00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:08.457
like they get fourth in all three,

250
00:09:08.457 --> 00:09:10.070
you think that's great,

251
00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.699
but it actually, they would do worse

252
00:09:11.699 --> 00:09:13.990
than someone who was a great speed climber

253
00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.660
but not as good as the other two disciplines.

254
00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.677
So it's this kind of weird formatting style

255
00:09:18.677 --> 00:09:22.740
that favors dominance in one category.

256
00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.090
And that's one of the reasons

257
00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:25.330
that a lot of climbers have complained

258
00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.710
about speed climbing being included,

259
00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.960
because most people focus on the other two aspects.

260
00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.188
Most people focus on bouldering and lead climbing

261
00:09:32.188 --> 00:09:35.350
and sort of exclude speed calming.

262
00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.520
And so by combining them all

263
00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.810
